cartridge "THE SIGNAL/AMY & CLAUDE/2026"

' THE SIGNAL (prototype: one night)
' An original horror game by Amy & Claude for Amy Studio, 2026, in Amy.
'
' October 31, 1983, 11:40 PM. You run the night shift at radio station
' WKBS 1340 AM at the edge of a snowed-in town. A voice keeps cutting in
' on the dial, reading names. The people it names are never seen again.
' Tune the dial until the signal comes clear: it tells you where it will
' strike next. Drive there through the dark, go in by flashlight and find
' the tape it left before it reads the name. Three names tonight. Then
' one more.
'
' Screens:
' - THE STATION: the radio panel (dial and needle, oscilloscope, two VU
'   meters), the logbook, a window onto the street. The stick tunes, the
'   left button listens, the right button goes out to the car.
' - THE TOWN: a top-down map of snowy streets, houses with lit windows,
'   streetlamps. Only the cells round the car are lit (signal.asm). Drive
'   to the house the signal named; the left button goes in at a door, or
'   back into the station at its door.
' - A HOUSE: a room seen in a flashlight circle. Find the tape (the left
'   button picks it up), then leave by the door at the bottom.
' The thing is never drawn clearly: at most a shadow at the edge of the
' light for half a second. The noise channel grows as the deadline nears,
' and now and then every sound stops for a few seconds.
'
' The voice is VoxPCM (Amy's adaptive PCM voice), made from a small
' formant synthesizer (voice/speak.py, voice/enc.mjs): real recordings put
' in voice/rec/ replace it.
'
' House rules kept: joystick only, tiles from code 128, text in columns
' 2-29, every screen drawn with the NMI off after a wait, set sprite
' count, nothing flashes faster than 3 times a second, at the end a press
' returns to the title (the screen sleeps after 30 seconds).

